course: dictionary
lesson: 11519
title: The alimentary canal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are only used in one subject. «Alimentary» is a science word, and you will meet it when you learn about the human body. It means to do with food and digestion.
explain: Look for the words around it to help you. «Food moves along the alimentary canal, from the mouth to the bottom.» The clue is the word canal, which means a long tube. So an alimentary canal is a long tube that food travels through.
explain: The alimentary canal includes the gullet, the stomach and the intestines. «The stomach is part of the alimentary canal.» You can check your meaning by swapping it in: «The stomach is part of the food and digestion tube.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Alimentary means to do with food and digestion.
fact: Digestion is the process of breaking down food so the body can use it.
fact: The alimentary canal is the long tube from the mouth to the bottom.
fact: The gullet, stomach and intestines are all parts of the alimentary canal.
fact: «Alimentary» is mostly used in the phrase «alimentary canal».
exercise: «Food moves along the alimentary canal, from the mouth to the bottom.» What does alimentary mean? | To do with light and colour | To do with breathing and air | *To do with food and digestion | To do with bones and muscles
exercise: Which of these is part of the alimentary canal? | *The stomach | The lungs | The brain | The heart
exercise: In «alimentary canal», which word tells you what the thing is? | *canal | neither word | alimentary | both words
test: «The doctor explained how food is digested in the alimentary canal.» What does the alimentary canal do? | It makes our bones strong | It helps us hear sounds | *It digests food, from the mouth to the bottom | It pumps blood around the body
test: Which word means to do with food and digestion? | Luminous | Curt | *Alimentary | Ancient
exam: Which tube takes food from the mouth down to the bottom? | Spinal cord | Windpipe | Blood vessel | *Alimentary canal
